From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 17:11:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tools: build `lex` and `yacc` on a non-illumos host

`usr/src/tools/{lex,yacc}` exist to give a cross-build the gate's own
scanner and parser generators, which `Makefile.master` then names as
`$(ONBLD_TOOLS)/bin/$(MACH)/{lex,yacc}`. They do not build on a host
without illumos headers, because both include `<widec.h>`.

`<widec.h>` is `<wchar.h>` plus the EUC codeset machinery and the
pre-standard "wide string" functions. lex and yacc use only five of the
latter -- `wslen`, `wscpy`, `wscmp`, `wsprintf` and `watoi` -- and
otherwise want nothing the host's `<wchar.h>` does not already provide.

Add a `<widec.h>` shim under `cmd/sgs/include`, which both tool Makefiles
already put on the include path as `-I$(SGSDIR)/include`, so no Makefile
changes are needed. It maps those five onto their ISO C equivalents.
`wsprintf` is the only one that is not a rename: it takes a *narrow*
format string and emits wide characters, so `swprintf` is not a drop-in
and the shim formats narrow and widens the result.

Where a real `<widec.h>` exists it is used unchanged, via
`__has_include_next`. That test, rather than `#ifdef __sun`, is what makes
this work: `Makefile.master` passes `-D__sun` to the *native* compiles as
well as the target ones, so `__sun` says nothing about which libc's
headers are in front of the compiler.

Assisted-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
